        "collapsible_tab_UWQ8gk": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Overview",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Overview",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<h3>Built for the Slope Nothing Else Can Take</h3><p>Loose soil, wet grass, drainage banks, hillside beds, the <strong>Mowrator S1 21″ 4WD Grip Tread Tire Edition</strong> is built to go where the rest of the S1 lineup stops.</p><p>Full-time <strong>4WD</strong> and <strong>Grip Tread deformable tires</strong> combine to handle slopes up to <strong>100% grade (45°)</strong>, the highest slope rating in the entire S1 platform.</p><p>The <strong>21″ cutting deck</strong> and adjustable cutting height give you control over the cut, while the <strong>18Ah Steady Force battery</strong> gives you up to <strong>2.25 hours</strong> of runtime and <strong>1.125 acres</strong> per charge.</p><p><strong>Mow, mulch, bag, or discharge</strong>, all from a safe, comfortable distance with the included remote controller.</p><p><strong>The steepest yard on the block isn't a problem anymore. It's just another Tuesday.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_Uf69Wz": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Product Information",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Product Information",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<h2>Battery & Runtime</h2><p>The Grip Tread Tire Edition ships in a single configuration: a 56V 18Ah LiFePO4 “Steady Force” battery, delivering up to <strong>2.25 hours</strong> of runtime and coverage of up to <strong>1.125 acres</strong> per charge — sized for the extra draw of sustained climbing.</p><h2>Cutting Power</h2><p>The 21″ steel cutting deck offers adjustable cutting height from <strong>1.5″ to 4.3″</strong>, with mulch, rear bag, or side discharge options depending on the job.</p><h2>Drive & Traction</h2><p>Full-time 4WD distributes power across all four wheels, and the included <strong>Grip Tread deformable tires</strong> flex to maintain contact on loose, uneven, or steep ground. Together they're rated for slopes up to <strong>100% grade (45°)</strong> — the highest of any S1 configuration, ahead of the standard 4WD (75% / 37°) and Wide Wheels (85% / 40°) editions.</p><h2>Control</h2><p>The S1 is operated via handheld remote control rather than autonomous navigation, so you stay in command of every pass — especially on terrain where unattended operation isn't the right call.</p><h2>Warranty</h2><p>2 year warranty covering the main machine, remote, and battery.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_X7L37G": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Warranty & Support",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Warranty & Support",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Every Mowrator S1 4WD Grip Tread Tire Edition is backed by Mowrator's standard 2 year warranty, covering the main machine, the remote control, and the battery.</p><p><strong>What's covered</strong><br/><br/>Manufacturing defects and functional failures under normal residential use. Warranty service is handled through Mowrator's authorized repair network; you'll need proof of purchase (order date, model, and serial number) to file a claim.</p><p><strong>30 Day Money-Back Guarantee</strong><br/><br/>If the Grip Tread Edition doesn't work out for your terrain, return it within 30 days of delivery for a refund. Keep the original packaging on hand for the return window — it makes the process faster.</p><p><strong>Reporting an issue</strong><br/><br/>Inspect your mower on delivery. Shipping damage should be reported within 24 hours, and any other concerns within 7 days, to keep your claim eligible.</p><p><strong>Our role</strong><br/><br/>As your dealer, we're your first point of contact. Reach out to us for setup help, order questions, or to get a warranty claim started, and we'll coordinate directly with Mowrator on your behalf so you're not left navigating it alone.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_HjeTwa": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Setup & Installation",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Setup & Installation",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Getting the Grip Tread Tire Edition running takes about 15 to 20 minutes, most of it charging.</p><p><strong>In the box</strong><br/><br/>Mower body with 21 inch cutting deck, Steady Force 18Ah battery, 600W Fast Super Charger, Professional Remote Controller, Grip Tread deformable tires (installed), manual grass bag with frame, and standard tool/data accessories.</p><p><strong>1. Charge the battery</strong><br/><br/>Before first use, fully charge the battery using the included 600W charger. Connect the charger to a standard outlet and seat the battery securely in the charging port.</p><p><strong>2. Assemble the grass bag</strong><br/><br/>Check the bag for damage before installing. Slide the fabric onto the metal frame, then fasten the rubber strips around the bag opening to the frame.</p><p><strong>3. Choose your clipping mode</strong><br/><br/>For mulching, open the grass outlet cover and insert the mulching insert. For bagging, attach the assembled grass bag. For discharge, no attachment is needed.</p><p><strong>4. Seat the battery</strong><br/><br/>Unlock the battery buckle, insert the battery into its compartment until secure, and close the buckle.</p><p><strong>5. Pair the remote</strong><br/><br/>Power on the mower. The remote connects to it wirelessly. Indicator lights confirm connection status: red means not connected, amber means connecting, green means ready to mow.</p><p><strong>6. Set your cutting height</strong><br/><br/>Adjust the deck to your starting height within the 1.5 to 4.3 inch range. Start higher on the first cut, especially on steep or uneven ground.</p><p><strong>7. Walk the slope before you mow it</strong><br/><br/>Before running the mower on a steep section, walk it yourself first. Clear sticks, rocks, and debris that could catch the tires. Keep people and pets clear of the mowing area, and always mow across a slope, not straight up or down it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_czbJiW": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Specifications",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Specifications",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Model: Mowrator S1 21″ 4WD Grip Tread Tire Edition<br/><br/>Drive: Four-wheel drive (4WD)<br/><br/>Tires: Grip Tread deformable tires<br/><br/>Cutting width: 21 in<br/><br/>Cutting height range: 1.5 to 4.3 in, adjustable<br/><br/>Max slope rating: 100% grade (45°)<br/><br/>Battery: 56V LiFePO4, 18Ah (Steady Force)<br/><br/>Runtime: up to 2.25 hours<br/><br/>Coverage per charge: up to 1.125 acres<br/><br/>Charger: 600W Fast Super Charger<br/><br/>Clipping system: mulch, rear bag, or side discharge<br/><br/>Control method: handheld remote control<br/><br/>Warranty: 2 years on main machine, remote control, and battery<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
